# Line-ending discipline for files whose contents must never gain CRLF.
#
# core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) converts LF->CRLF on checkout. For a
# shell script, that breaks the shebang: the kernel reads "#!/bin/sh\r" and
# cannot find the interpreter. The 0A.13 node entrypoint (docker/nginx-node-1/
# entrypoint.sh) and generate_keys.sh must stay LF, or a fresh clone on Windows
# builds a node image that crashes on start. Dockerfiles and the sshd_config are
# pinned for the same reason: Docker/OpenSSH tolerate CRLF poorly.

*.sh                 text eol=lf
Dockerfile           text eol=lf
ssh/sshd_config      text eol=lf
**/ssh/sshd_config   text eol=lf
